# `list[i] == 100.5` in a loop over what is written number[]. Link has proven of the elements fractions, and objects of which nothing is known: that says nothing, so the guess at an element of numbers opens.
# Of what Int32 storage holds nothing is left beside that proof, so no run comes behind its two tests. That ends this one way: Double storage is asked in its turn, and the typed run reads a double.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: [[int32]]: boolean @Boolean = HasArrayStorage [[list]] arrayStorage=Int32
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[int32]] -> taken [[present]](), notTaken [[other]]()
# CHECK: [[other]]() isInLoop=true:
# CHECK-NEXT: [[double]]: boolean @Boolean = HasArrayStorage [[list]] arrayStorage=Double
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[double]] ->
# CHECK: : never @Int32 = GetArrayElement [[list]], {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32
# CHECK: Unreachable
# CHECK: : fractional @Double = GetArrayElement [[list]], {{*}}arrayStorage=Double
